From: knoopx <knoopx@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] int3472: force 24 MHz mclk for the GC5035 sensor

The CHUWI Hi10 Max front GC5035 sensor needs a 24 MHz master clock, but
the firmware SSDB (the LNK1 ACPI device, whose _HID resolves to GCTI5035)
reports a 19.2 MHz MCLK (the L1CK crystal) in its MCLKSPEED DWord at SSDB
offset 86. skl_int3472_get_clk_frequency() reads that DWord, so the
int3472 per-sensor clock reports 19.2 MHz and the gc5035 driver logs
"mclk rate set to 19200000 instead of requested ...".

Force the reported rate to 24000000 for the GC5035 sensor (HID GCTI5035)
so the int3472 clock and the gc5035 mclk both read 24000000. This is a
reporting override: if the physical crystal is genuinely 19.2 MHz the
sensor may still not stream (hardware limit).

The sensor's ACPI HID is matched with acpi_dev_hid_match() from
<acpi/acpi_bus.h>: int3472->sensor is a struct acpi_device * (see
struct int3472_discrete_device in <linux/platform_data/x86/int3472.h>),
which is exactly what the matcher takes. acpi_dev_hid_match() is stable
API in 7.2.8.

7.2.8-adapted from the 6.18.54 series: the v7.0 clk_and_regulator.c
skl_int3472_get_clk_frequency() carries an early-return IS_ERR check and
a buffer-length guard that the 6.18.54 version lacked, so the hunk line
numbers differ (the force block lands after kfree(obj) at line 97, not
the 6.18.54 position). The force-block body is unchanged. The explicit
<acpi/acpi_bus.h> include is placed AFTER <linux/acpi.h>: the v7.0 file
already includes <linux/acpi.h>, which pulls in <acpi/acpi.h> (the ACPICA
wrapper that defines acpi_handle et al.) and <acpi/acpi_bus.h> itself,
while <acpi/acpi_bus.h> alone does not provide the ACPICA types —
including it first breaks the out-of-tree build.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
---
 clk_and_regulator.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/clk_and_regulator.c b/clk_and_regulator.c
--- a/clk_and_regulator.c
+++ b/clk_and_regulator.c
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
 /* Author: Dan Scally <djrscally@gmail.com> */
 
 #include <linux/acpi.h>
+#include <acpi/acpi_bus.h>
 #include <linux/clkdev.h>
 #include <linux/clk-provider.h>
@@ -9,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <linux/platform_data/x86/int3472.h>
 #include <linux/regulator/driver.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
+#include <linux/string.h>
 
 /*
  * 82c0d13a-78c5-4244-9bb1-eb8b539a8d11
@@ -97,6 +99,16 @@
 	freq = *(u32 *)(obj->buffer.pointer + CIO2_SENSOR_SSDB_MCLKSPEED_OFFSET);
 
 	kfree(obj);
+
+	/*
+	 * CHUWI Hi10 Max GC5035: the firmware SSDB (LNK1.SSDB) reports a 19.2 MHz
+	 * MCLK (the L1CK crystal), but the GC5035 sensor needs 24 MHz. Force the
+	 * reported rate for the GC5035 so the int3472 per-sensor clock and the
+	 * gc5035 mclk both read 24000000.
+	 */
+	if (acpi_dev_hid_match(int3472->sensor, "GCTI5035"))
+		freq = 24000000;
+
 	return freq;
 }
